<h2>Which Is Better: Under Desk Bike or Elliptical?</h2>
<p>Use these rules of thumb to settle the under desk elliptical vs bike decision.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Choose an under desk elliptical</strong> if your desk is standard height or lower, you want to pedal for hours while typing, you have sensitive knees, or you are a senior looking for gentle movement. See our <a href="/best-under-desk-elliptical-for-seniors/">best under desk elliptical for seniors</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Choose an under desk bike</strong> if you have generous knee room, you want higher resistance for short, harder sessions, and you are comfortable with a cycling motion.</li>
<li><strong>Choose a desk bike with its own desk</strong> if you want a real cardio session while you work and have floor space to spare.</li>
</ul>
<p>Still unsure? Our <a href="/tools/which-under-desk-elliptical-quiz/">under desk elliptical quiz</a> asks about your desk, goals and noise needs and points you to a model. You can also browse every model in the <a href="/tools/compare-under-desk-ellipticals/">comparison tool</a>.</p>

<h2>Verdict: Under Desk Elliptical vs Bike</h2>
<p>For most people, the under desk elliptical is the better daily companion than a desk bike. It clears more desks, feels smoother on the knees and fades into the background while you work, which means you will use it more. The [[amazon:cubii-jr2|Cubii JR2]] is our top pick for quiet, all-day use.</p>
<p>If you want more of a workout and have room under your desk, the [[amazon:deskcycle-2|DeskCycle 2 under desk bike]] gives you more resistance to work against. Whichever you choose, start with short sessions and light resistance. Our guide on <a href="/how-to-use-under-desk-elliptical/">how to use an under desk elliptical</a> covers setup, posture and a first-week plan.</p>
